WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.235 --> 00:00:23.330
Iris ran toward the soccer goal, her feet dribbling the ball with perfect control.

2
00:00:23.331 --> 00:00:31.602
The scent of fresh-cut grass filled her nose as she sped forward. It gave her a burst of energy.

3
00:00:31.603 --> 00:00:38.650
She faked to the right and then twisted her body left for a direct shot.

4
00:00:38.651 --> 00:00:46.240
Bam! The ball soared past the goalie's fingertips and into the net.

5
00:00:46.241 --> 00:00:50.985
"Score!" Jake high-fived Iris.

6
00:00:50.986 --> 00:00:55.395
His hand felt as hot and sweaty as her own.

7
00:00:55.396 --> 00:01:01.813
After all that running around, she hoped she didn't smell too terrible.

8
00:01:01.814 --> 00:01:10.807
"Yes!" Sophia jumped up and down at Iris' side, her dark ponytail bouncing with her.

9
00:01:10.808 --> 00:01:16.060
Iris grinned. The three of them made a great team.

10
00:01:16.061 --> 00:01:24.696
Now that seventh grade was over for the year, they were free to play soccer in the park every afternoon if they wanted to.

11
00:01:24.697 --> 00:01:30.949
No homework, no projects, no after-school activities.

12
00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:40.036
The best possible summer lay ahead, filled with many more sunny afternoons and soccer games like this one.

13
00:01:40.037 --> 00:01:48.020
"Game's over!" the goalie said. "You guys won today, but we'll beat you next week."

14
00:01:48.021 --> 00:01:56.685
"What time is it?" Jake asked. He patted his pockets, looking for his phone.

15
00:01:56.686 --> 00:01:58.930
But they were empty.

16
00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:06.517
Iris shrugged. The sun still hung above the treetops, so it couldn't be that late.

17
00:02:06.518 --> 00:02:13.914
She watched as Sophia jogged over to the sideline and dug through her soccer bag for her phone.

18
00:02:13.915 --> 00:02:19.649
Iris had told her friends that her mom wouldn't let her have a phone until high school.

19
00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:27.245
But the truth was, Mama couldn't afford phones for Iris and her twin brother, Javier.

20
00:02:27.245 --> 00:02:33.385
Mama could barely afford her own phone since Papa had left the family last year.

21
00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:39.472
Sometimes Iris missed Papa's shooting goals with her on Sunday mornings.

22
00:02:39.473 --> 00:02:44.490
Mostly, though, things were easier without him around.

23
00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:50.310
Across the field Sophia pulled her phone out of her bag.

24
00:02:50.311 --> 00:02:52.211
"It's six o'clock!"

25
00:02:52.212 --> 00:03:02.791
"Already?" Iris clapped a hand over her mouth. "I've got to go. Great game, everyone!" she yelled as she ran off the field.

26
00:03:02.792 --> 00:03:07.659
"See you tomorrow, Iris!" Sophia called after her.

27
00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:13.534
Without looking back, Iris waved and sped for home.

28
00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:19.003
Home for Iris was a brick apartment building two blocks from the park.

29
00:03:19.004 --> 00:03:25.683
Iris turned her key in the front lock and raced up to the third floor.

30
00:03:25.683 --> 00:03:34.340
She opened the door to her family's apartment as quietly as possible, but Javier had already spotted her.

31
00:03:34.341 --> 00:03:40.601
Her brother looked up from his computer screen. "You're late," he said.

32
00:03:40.602 --> 00:03:49.848
Iris scowled. "It's easier to get home on time if you're always here, playing with imaginary friends on the computer!"

33
00:03:49.849 --> 00:03:56.355
As usual, Javier was doing something online.

34
00:03:56.356 --> 00:04:01.663
This was why his skin was at least two shades lighter than hers.

35
00:04:01.664 --> 00:04:11.497
Other than that, the twins actually looked a lot alike, with the same dark eyes, full lips, and frizzy curls.

36
00:04:11.498 --> 00:04:21.817
"It's called gaming, not playing." Javier looked back at the screen. "Anyway, Mama's furious at you."

37
00:04:21.818 --> 00:04:32.305
Just then footsteps pounded down the hall from the kitchen. "Iris? Are you here?" Mama's eyes blazed.

38
00:04:32.306 --> 00:04:40.392
"Finally! I was worried about you. Don't scare me like that again, young lady."

39
00:04:40.393 --> 00:04:43.825
"Mama, I was only ten minutes late."

40
00:04:43.825 --> 00:04:54.107
"No matter. This is why we have rules in this household, and this is why you're going to—" She pressed her lips together.

41
00:04:54.108 --> 00:04:58.017
"Never mind. I'll tell you more at dinner.

42
00:04:58.018 --> 00:05:05.453
Time to set the table." She thundered back down the hall.

43
00:05:05.454 --> 00:05:10.751
"Uh-oh," Iris whispered. "What was that about?"

44
00:05:10.752 --> 00:05:15.336
Javier shrugged. "I guess we'll find out."

45
00:05:15.336 --> 00:05:26.588
A few minutes later, the twins went into the kitchen, where the scents of cilantro, garlic, and tomato rose from a pot of beans simmering on the stove.

46
00:05:26.589 --> 00:05:33.332
Mama scooped rice into bowls, topping each with a big spoonful of beans.

47
00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:41.318
Javier poured water into tall glasses, and Iris got out forks and napkins.

48
00:05:41.319 --> 00:05:48.341
No one spoke, but Iris could hear their neighbor playing his flamenco guitar again.

49
00:05:48.342 --> 00:05:58.071
Listening to the music usually relaxed her quickly, but tonight she was nervous about what Mama had to say.

50
00:05:58.072 --> 00:06:00.817
Iris slipped into her seat.

51
00:06:00.818 --> 00:06:06.957
The three of them ate in silence for a few minutes.

52
00:06:06.958 --> 00:06:10.545
Finally Mama cleared her throat.

53
00:06:10.546 --> 00:06:22.390
"I have some news to share," she said. "I got a new job, and it's a good one, working full-time in an office as a receptionist."

54
00:06:22.391 --> 00:06:26.125
"That's great, Mama!" Javier said.

55
00:06:26.126 --> 00:06:30.797
"Yes." Iris nodded and smiled at her mother.

56
00:06:30.797 --> 00:06:37.112
A full-time job was just what Mama needed—and in an office!

57
00:06:37.113 --> 00:06:44.890
Mama had been getting by cleaning houses in the mornings, but she was smart and good with people.

58
00:06:44.891 --> 00:06:48.871
The office job sounded perfect for her.

59
00:06:48.872 --> 00:06:51.458
Mama's eyes sparkled.

60
00:06:51.459 --> 00:07:00.365
"I'll get to dress up for work instead of having to wear sloppy clothes and sneakers, and I'll have my own desk and computer.

61
00:07:00.366 --> 00:07:03.759
I can't wait to start."

62
00:07:03.759 --> 00:07:07.650
"When is your first day?" Iris asked.

63
00:07:07.651 --> 00:07:11.602
"That's the other thing I needed to tell you."

64
00:07:11.602 --> 00:07:19.339
Mama looked down at her bowl. "I start on Monday, and as I said, it's a full-time job.

65
00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:23.574
I can't leave the two of you here alone all day long."

66
00:07:23.575 --> 00:07:28.985
"Why not?" Iris frowned. "We're 13 years old."

67
00:07:28.986 --> 00:07:33.569
"Almost 14," Javier added.

68
00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:39.647
Mama waggled a finger at them. "Your birthday is not until November!

69
00:07:39.648 --> 00:07:44.072
Staying home alone for this much time is not up for discussion.

70
00:07:44.073 --> 00:07:48.902
Besides, I've already signed you up for a camp."

71
00:07:48.903 --> 00:07:52.497
"Camp?" Javier made a face.

72
00:07:52.498 --> 00:07:55.475
Iris smirked at Javier.

73
00:07:55.475 --> 00:08:01.384
"I guess you'll actually have to go outside this summer!" Then she looked at her mother.

74
00:08:01.385 --> 00:08:05.730
"What kind of camp is it, Mama? Soccer camp, I hope?"

75
00:08:05.731 --> 00:08:17.282
"I'm sorry." Mama shook her head. "With such late notice, the only camp that still had two openings was tennis camp."

76
00:08:17.283 --> 00:08:21.361
"Huh?" Javier's mouth dropped open.

77
00:08:21.362 --> 00:08:27.277
"Tennis camp?" Iris slumped back on her chair.

78
00:08:27.277 --> 00:08:34.528
She didn't know many kids who played tennis. Her friends mostly liked soccer and basketball.

79
00:08:34.529 --> 00:08:47.525
Mama's gaze flitted between them. "You're both very lucky. A lot of kids would love to attend a camp like this. I'm sure it'll be lots of fun."

80
00:08:47.526 --> 00:08:54.670
When Mama put it like that, they couldn't argue anymore. But tennis camp?

81
00:08:54.671 --> 00:09:02.251
Iris shared a worried glance with Javier. Javier hated outdoor sports, period.

82
00:09:02.252 --> 00:09:06.645
And she had zero interest in learning how to play tennis.

83
00:09:06.646 --> 00:09:18.007
Iris' "perfect" summer didn't seem so perfect anymore.
